# Audit Timestamps & Optimistic Versioning

Source of truth: `docs/architecture/persistence.md` (audit/version section).

Kernel bases live in `packages/infrastructure/postgres/src/kernel/persistence/`.

## Base entities

| Base | Columns | Use for |
|------|---------|---------|
| `AuditableEntity` | `created_at`, `updated_at` (`timestamptz`) | **Every** production table row |
| `VersionedEntity` | above + `@VersionColumn()` `version` | Parent rows of child-collection aggregates |

```typescript
// ✅ All new TypeORM entities extend a kernel base
@Entity('users')
export class UserEntity extends AuditableEntity {
  @PrimaryColumn('uuid') id!: string
  // …
}

@Entity('roles')
export class RoleEntity extends VersionedEntity {
  @PrimaryColumn('uuid') id!: string
  // …
}
```

**Versioned parents today:** `RoleEntity`, `MembershipEntity`.  
**Auditable-only parents with child rows:** `InvitationEntity` (roles replaced via join table).  
**Child join tables** (`role_permissions`, `membership_roles`, `invitation_roles`) also extend `AuditableEntity`.

## Domain stays pure

Audit/version columns are **infrastructure-only**. Do **not** add `version`, `createdAt`, or `updatedAt` to domain aggregates, ports, or application commands. Mappers ignore them on read; writers stamp them on save.

## Writes

### Single-table repos

Use `manager.save(Entity, mapped)` — **not** `upsert`. Repositories join the ambient transaction via `transactionAls` (see `persistence.mdc`).

### Parent + child-collection repos

`Role`, `Membership`, and `Invitation` saves go through `ChildCollectionWriter`:

- **`saveVersionedParentAndReplaceChildren`** — versioned parent (`Role`, `Membership`); maps `OptimisticLockVersionMismatchError` → `OptimisticConcurrencyError`
- **`saveAuditableParentAndReplaceChildren`** — auditable parent only (`Invitation`)

Both paths:

1. Require an ambient `UnitOfWork` transaction (`AssertAmbientTransaction.assert()`)
2. `SELECT … FOR UPDATE` on the parent row before write
3. Preserve `createdAt` (and `version` for versioned) from the locked row
4. Delete + insert child rows (full collection replace)

Use cases that mutate these aggregates **must** wrap `save` in `uow.run()`. Test seeds/helpers too (`runInUnitOfWork`, or inject `UNIT_OF_WORK`).

```typescript
// ✅ application use case
await this.uow.run(async () => {
  await this.roles.save(role)
})

// ❌ repository save outside UoW — throws AmbientTransactionRequiredError
await this.roles.save(role)
```

## Migrations

New tables:

- Add `created_at` / `updated_at` (`timestamptz`, `NOT NULL`, sensible default/backfill for existing rows)
- Add `version` (`integer`, `NOT NULL`, default `1`) only on versioned parent tables

Register migrations in `postgres-migrations.ts`. Never hand-roll audit columns on entities without a matching migration.

## Tenant reads with explicit `tenantId`

When a repo method accepts `tenantId` but may run **without** ambient tenant scope (e.g. `findByUserAndTenant` for select-tenant), call `assertTenant(tenantId)` only if `hasEstablishedTenantScope()` — not when context is unset.

## Anti-patterns

```typescript
// ❌ Manual timestamp columns on entities
@CreateDateColumn() createdAt!: Date // extend AuditableEntity instead

// ❌ Domain aggregate carrying ORM version
class Role { constructor(readonly version: number) {} }

// ❌ Child-collection save without parent lock / UoW
await manager.save(parent)
await manager.delete(children)
```
